{"matches":[{"vulnerability":{"id":"GO-2026-6612","dataSource":"https://go.dev/cl/847187","namespace":"govulndb:language:go","severity":"Critical","urls":["https://go.dev/cl/847310","https://go.dev/issue/81743","https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/U2fTuyDJznI","https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/ZPwCyRUuGBs"],"description":"The HTTP/2 server can refund connection-level flow control twice for the same data: Once when a client resets a stream (refunding data for any sent-but-unread portion of the stream), and again when a request handler reads the buffered data. A malicious client can exploit this to bypass the configured connection-level flow control limit (MaxReceiveBufferPerConnection). Total buffered data is still limited by the concurrent stream limit and stream-level flow control.","cvss":[{"source":"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":9.1,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":5.2},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-78663","epss":0.00622,"percentile":0.49991,"date":"2026-11-06"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-78663","cwe":"CWE-675","source":"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["0.60.0"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"0.60.0","date":"2026-10-08","kind":"release"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.56291},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-78663","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-78663","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Critical","urls":["https://go.dev/cl/847187","https://go.dev/cl/847310","https://go.dev/issue/81743","https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/U2fTuyDJznI","https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/ZPwCyRUuGBs","https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-6612"],"description":"The HTTP/2 server can refund connection-level flow control twice for the same data: Once when a client resets a stream (refunding data for any sent-but-unread po